From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tatsuki Tanaka <tatsuki@tanakatatsuki.dev>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 09:54:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: iris: WIP VPU2 (SM8450/SM8475) HFI Gen2 encoder
 support

vpu20_4v.mbn speaks HFI Gen2, not Gen1. Switch sm8450 to a Gen2 firmware
data variant, add encoder BUF_DPB (required by VPU2, dropped on VPU3),
skip WRAPPER_TZ_* writes on power-off (TZ-protected on SM8450/SM8475),
fix encoder port->plane mapping on session stop, and log more detail on
session info/error packets.

Decoder works; encoder START is still rejected by firmware without DPB,
and the DPB variant is suspected to hard-reset the SoC (unconfirmed).

---
